<title>NETHERLANDS: VAN DORP NARROWS H1 LOSS.</title>
<headline>VAN DORP NARROWS H1 LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>NIEUWEGEIN, Neerlands 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss per shr (guilders)	2.19 vs   2.41 </p>
<p>    Net loss				 2.95 vs   3.24</p>
<p>    Turnover				95.59 vs 105.49</p>
<p>    Operating loss			 2.82 vs   1.22</p>
<p>    Tax					1.74 vs   1.34</p>
<p>    Extraordinary charges		NIL  vs   1.43</p>
<p>NOTE - Office supplies group Van Dorp said it expected to</p>
<p>return to operating profit in the second half of this year, but</p>
<p>added that the expected sale of subsidiaries and a planned</p>
<p>merger with Jonkers Holding made it impossible to give a firm</p>
<p>profit forecast for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
